@* Ported from Index.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs.

   CONTENT-FREE BY ORIGIN, verified: the .ascx carried ONLY the license comment and the
   <%@ Control %> directive, the designer declared no fields, and OnControlLoad's body was
   empty. The legacy screen rendered an empty region; emitting markup would ADD a screen the
   module never had. The entire server-side behaviour is the base's logging plus
   CheckAccessLevel + CheckTransactionPostingStatus, which MixERPUserControl runs for every
   control.

   The original declared no OverridePath, AccessLevel, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme or
   IsLandingPage override and implemented no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control declares it.
    ///     The legacy body was ALREADY EMPTY (see above) - there is nothing to port into it.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }
}
